  "solution": {
    "text": "In a <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></math> sum of two sides should be greater then the third side<br /><br />It is given that <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></math> is isosceles<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Total cases in which isosceles <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></math> will come is<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>